course: dictionary
lesson: 12632
title: Disobey and the prefix dis-
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To obey means to do what you are told. To disobey means the opposite: to not do what a person, a rule or a law tells you to do. The small part dis- at the start often means not, so disobey means not obey.
explain: «Mum said to stay on the path, but Sam went into the woods. He disobeyed her.» Mum told Sam what to do, and he did the opposite. Disobeyed is the past tense, because it happened before now.
explain: The word family has four forms: disobey, disobeys, disobeyed, disobeying. Other words with dis- also mean not, such as dislike and dishonest. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence: «He did not do what Mum said.» If it still makes sense, you are right.
fact: Disobey means to not do what a person, rule or law tells you to do.
fact: The prefix dis- at the start of a word often means not, so disobey means not obey.
fact: «The sign said keep off the ice, but the boy disobeyed it and walked out.» Here the sign is a safety rule, and the boy did not follow it.
fact: The verb forms are disobey, disobeys, disobeyed and disobeying.
fact: In many fairy tales, the hero gets into trouble when they disobey a warning, and the Bible says Adam and Eve disobeyed God.
exercise: «The lifeguard told the children to stay out of the deep water, but Tom swam out anyway.» What did Tom do? | *He disobeyed the lifeguard | He swam back to the beach | He asked the lifeguard for a drink | He obeyed the lifeguard and stayed on the sand
exercise: Which word means not do what you are told? | listen | shout | *disobey | wander
exercise: Fill the gap: «The dog ___ its owner and ran onto the busy road.» | *disobeyed | disobeying | obeyed | disobey
test: «Safety rules keep us safe. If you disobey the road rule and cross when the light is red, you put yourself in danger.» What does disobey mean here? | Read the rule aloud | Shout at the rule | *Not do what the rule tells you to do | Do what you are told
test: Which word is the past tense of disobey? | disobeying | *disobeyed | disobey | disobeys
exam: Ruby says disobey means to do what you are told. Is she right? | Yes, because obey means not | Yes, dis- means do | *No, disobey means not doing what you are told | No, because it is a noun
